<article class="env-definition" id="05G4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05G4">Definition <span data-tag="05G4">10.14.1</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : R \to S$ be a ring map. Let $M$ be an $S$-module. Let $R \to R'$ be any ring map. The <em>base change</em> of $\varphi $ by $R \to R'$ is the ring map $R' \to S \otimes _ R R'$. In this situation we often write $S' = S \otimes _ R R'$. The <em>base change</em> of the $S$-module $M$ is the $S'$-module $M \otimes _ R R'$. </p>
</article>